"""
The standard library's `RotationalEMF` with its flux as an input: `k` is KΦ at full flux, and
`field` scales Φ.

    v = field k w        tau = -field k i

`field` is the flux as a fraction of its full value, 1 for full flux. It scales the back-EMF and
the torque per ampere by the same factor, so the power balance `v i = -tau w` holds at every
`field`, as it does for the fixed-flux element. The pins, splines, variables and sign conventions
are those of `RotationalEMF`, so the two swap without other changes; with `field = 1` they are
the same element.

Turning `field` down is field weakening (deck 7 slide 26: "changing the magnetic flux Φ"). In a
wound-field DC machine the field current sets Φ; in a permanent-magnet machine under
field-oriented control the inverter weakens the magnets' flux with its d-axis current. This
element covers either at the level of the DC-equivalent machine: Φ is whatever the controller
asks for, with no cost of its own. A real PM machine pays for weakening in d-axis copper loss,
which this element does not carry.
"""
component FieldEMF
  "Positive electrical pin"
  p = Pin() {^p}
  "Negative electrical pin"
  n = Pin() {^n}
  "Rotor spline"
  rotor = Spline() {^rotor}
  "Housing (support) of the emf shaft"
  housing = Spline() {^housing}
  "Flux as a fraction of full flux, 1 for full"
  field = RealInput() {^field}
  "Torque and back-EMF constant KΦ at full flux"
  parameter k::ElectricalTorqueConstant
  "Voltage drop between the two pins"
  variable v::Voltage
  "Current flowing from positive to negative pin"
  variable i::Current
  "Angle of the rotor with respect to the housing"
  variable phi::Angle
  "Angular velocity of the rotor relative to the housing"
  variable w::AngularVelocity
  "Torque on the rotor"
  variable tau::Torque
relations
  v = p.v - n.v
  0 = p.i + n.i
  i = p.i
  phi = rotor.phi - housing.phi
  w = der(phi)
  v = field * k * w
  tau = -field * k * i
  tau = rotor.tau
  0 = housing.tau + rotor.tau
metadata {
  "Dyad": {
    "labels": [{"label": "$(instance)", "x": 500, "y": 1200, "rot": 0}],
    "icons": {"default": "dyad://ElectricalComponents/RotationalEMF.svg"}
  },
  "_links": {
    "p": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"iconName": "pos", "x1": 450, "y1": -50, "x2": 550, "y2": 50}}}},
    "n": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"iconName": "neg", "x1": 450, "y1": 950, "x2": 550, "y2": 1050}}}},
    "rotor": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"x1": 950, "y1": 450, "x2": 1050, "y2": 550}}}},
    "housing": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"x1": -50, "y1": 450, "x2": 50, "y2": 550}}}},
    "field": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"x1": 150, "y1": -50, "x2": 250, "y2": 50, "rot": 90}}}}
  }
}
end
